# Track 05 — Jinja2 HTML Report Template Patterns
**Stream:** B (Report Generation) · **Feeds:** `report/` package · **Status:** Research complete, no code committed (research-only track)

## 0. Scope Recap

Input data source is a `list[MetricResult]` (locked at M1, `src/bias_aperture/schema.py`):

```
metric_name, subgroup, subgroup_sample_size, metric_value,
ci_lower, ci_upper, p_value, insufficient_sample
```

`metric_name ∈ {demographic_parity_difference, equalized_odds_difference,
equal_opportunity_difference, disparate_impact_ratio}`. `insufficient_sample=True`
rows always carry `metric_value=None` (enforced in `MetricResult.__post_init__`,
NFR-003) — the template must render these as flagged rows, never as zeros or blanks
that look like a computed value.

Deliverable: Jinja2 template + CSS design covering the six requirements in the
track prompt, plus the Python-side data transformation that feeds it.

---

## 1. Recommended Package Layout

```
report/
├── generator.py            # build_context(), render_report(), filters
├── templates/
│   └── report.html.jinja   # single authoring template (may use Jinja2
│                            # {% macro %}/{% include %} internally — the
│                            # OUTPUT is one flat self-contained HTML file,
│                            # only the *source* is modular)
└── static/
    └── report.css          # dev-time source of truth for the CSS; inlined
                             # into <style> at render time, never linked
```

Keeping `report.css` as a real file (not a Python string literal) lets it be
linted/diffed normally; `generator.py` reads it once and injects it via
`{% raw %}`-safe string interpolation into the `<style>` block, so the shipped
artifact still has zero external `<link>` tags.

---

## 2. Jinja2 Environment Configuration

```python
from jinja2 import Environment, FileSystemLoader, select_autoescape

env = Environment(
    loader=FileSystemLoader("report/templates"),
    autoescape=select_autoescape(["html", "jinja2"]),  # HTML-escape all vars
    trim_blocks=True,     # strip newline after a block tag
    lstrip_blocks=True,   # strip leading whitespace before a block tag
)
```

- `autoescape=True` is non-negotiable even though `subgroup` strings are
  internally constructed from the locked label vocabulary (not raw user
  input) — defense-in-depth costs nothing and protects against a future
  ingestion path that isn't as clean.
- `trim_blocks`/`lstrip_blocks` keep the rendered HTML readable if a human
  ever opens it in a text editor (compliance reports get archived and
  diffed across audit runs).

---

## 3. Data Transformation Layer (`generator.py`)

The template stays "dumb" (formatting only); all grouping/ranking logic lives
in Python so it's unit-testable independent of HTML.

```python
from __future__ import annotations

import base64
from collections import defaultdict
from dataclasses import asdict
from pathlib import Path
from typing import Any

from bias_aperture.schema import ALPHA, MetricResult

METRIC_LABELS: dict[str, str] = {
    "demographic_parity_difference": "Demographic Parity Difference",
    "equalized_odds_difference": "Equalized Odds Difference",
    "equal_opportunity_difference": "Equal Opportunity Difference",
    "disparate_impact_ratio": "Disparate Impact Ratio",
}

# Shape only — content is Track 08's deliverable (see §9).
RegulatoryTag = dict[str, str]           # {"article": "10(2)(f)", "note": "..."}
RegulatoryMap = dict[str, list[RegulatoryTag]]  # keyed by metric_name


def row_status(row: MetricResult) -> str:
    """CSS status bucket for one row. Defensive on None even though
    __post_init__ already guarantees insufficient rows carry no value."""
    if row.insufficient_sample or row.metric_value is None:
        return "status-insufficient"
    if row.p_value is not None and row.p_value < ALPHA:
        return "status-significant"
    return "status-ok"


def deviation_from_fair(row: MetricResult) -> float:
    """Ranking key for 'worst subgroup'. disparate_impact_ratio's fair
    point is 1.0, not 0 — a naive abs(metric_value) ranking would be wrong
    for that metric specifically (Watkins et al. 2022 is exactly why this
    project never treats DIR as a bare number — see lit review matrix)."""
    if row.metric_value is None:
        return float("-inf")
    if row.metric_name == "disparate_impact_ratio":
        return abs(1.0 - row.metric_value)
    return abs(row.metric_value)


def group_by_metric(rows: list[MetricResult]) -> dict[str, list[MetricResult]]:
    grouped: dict[str, list[MetricResult]] = defaultdict(list)
    for r in rows:
        grouped[r.metric_name].append(r)
    return dict(grouped)


def metric_summary(rows: list[MetricResult]) -> dict[str, Any]:
    scored = [r for r in rows if row_status(r) != "status-insufficient"]
    significant = [r for r in scored if r.p_value is not None and r.p_value < ALPHA]
    worst = max(significant, key=deviation_from_fair, default=None)
    return {
        "dashboard_pass": len(significant) == 0,
        "n_significant": len(significant),
        "n_insufficient": sum(1 for r in rows if row_status(r) == "status-insufficient"),
        "n_total": len(rows),
        "worst_subgroup": worst,
    }


def image_to_data_uri(path: Path) -> str:
    """Inline a SHAP PNG as base64 so the report has zero external file
    references — required for the 'single self-contained file' spec."""
    encoded = base64.b64encode(path.read_bytes()).decode("ascii")
    return f"data:image/png;base64,{encoded}"


def build_context(
    rows: list[MetricResult],
    generated_at: str,
    regulatory_map: RegulatoryMap,
    shap_image_paths: dict[str, Path],  # key = f"{metric_name}::{subgroup}"
) -> dict[str, Any]:
    grouped = group_by_metric(rows)
    return {
        "generated_at": generated_at,
        "alpha": ALPHA,
        "metrics": [
            {
                "key": key,
                "label": METRIC_LABELS[key],
                "rows": grouped[key],
                "summary": metric_summary(grouped[key]),
                "regulatory": regulatory_map.get(key, []),
            }
            for key in METRIC_LABELS
            if key in grouped
        ],
        "shap_images": {k: image_to_data_uri(p) for k, p in shap_image_paths.items()},
    }


def render_report(context: dict[str, Any], env) -> str:
    env.filters["status_class"] = row_status
    env.filters["fmt_num"] = lambda v, d=3: "—" if v is None else f"{v:.{d}f}"
    env.filters["fmt_p"] = lambda v: (
        "—" if v is None else ("<0.001" if v < 0.001 else f"{v:.3f}")
    )
    env.filters["fmt_ci"] = lambda r: (
        "—" if r.ci_lower is None or r.ci_upper is None
        else f"[{r.ci_lower:.3f}, {r.ci_upper:.3f}]"
    )
    return env.get_template("report.html.jinja").render(**context)
```

`asdict` import left in deliberately — useful if a JSON sidecar export of the
same `MetricResult` list is added later (out of this track's scope; flagging
only).

---

## 4. Conditional Formatting Rules (locked mapping for the template)

| Condition | CSS class | Visual treatment | Badge text |
|---|---|---|---|
| `insufficient_sample=True` (or defensively, `metric_value is None`) | `status-insufficient` | grey row background, muted text | "— Insufficient sample" |
| `insufficient_sample=False` and `p_value < ALPHA` (0.05) | `status-significant` | red-tinted row background, bold text | "⚠ Disparity detected" |
| `insufficient_sample=False` and `p_value >= ALPHA` | `status-ok` | neutral/white row | "✓ No significant disparity" |

**Design note (flag, not a silent decision):** the track prompt asks for a
dashboard "pass/fail" per metric. This project's own literature review
(Watkins, McKenna & Chen 2022, "Four-Fifths Rule is Not Disparate Impact")
is the stated justification for *never* treating a bare number/threshold as
a compliance verdict (see `BiasAperture_NOVELTY_INTEGRATION_DEFENSE.md` and
`BiasAperture-AT.md` §12). To stay consistent with that project principle
while still satisfying the prompt's dashboard requirement, `dashboard_pass`
is implemented as a **scanning aid** (no significant subgroups found) with
a footer disclaimer, not a compliance certification — full per-subgroup
statistical detail is always one scroll away in the same document. This is
an interpretive convention, not part of the M1 schema lock — worth a
5-minute confirm with Aaradhya/Tisha before `report/generator.py` is built
for real.

---

## 5. Full Template — `report/templates/report.html.jinja`

```jinja
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
<title>BiasAperture Audit Report</title>
<style>
{{ inline_css }}
</style>
</head>
<body>

{% macro status_badge(status) -%}
  {%- if status == "status-significant" -%}
  <span class="badge badge-fail">&#9888; Disparity detected</span>
  {%- elif status == "status-insufficient" -%}
  <span class="badge badge-muted">&mdash; Insufficient sample</span>
  {%- else -%}
  <span class="badge badge-pass">&#10003; No significant disparity</span>
  {%- endif -%}
{%- endmacro %}

{% macro dashboard_card(metric) -%}
<div class="dash-card {{ 'dash-card-fail' if not metric.summary.dashboard_pass else 'dash-card-pass' }}">
  <h3><a href="#{{ metric.key }}">{{ metric.label }}</a></h3>
  {{ status_badge("status-significant" if not metric.summary.dashboard_pass else "status-ok") }}
  <p class="dash-meta">
    {{ metric.summary.n_significant }} significant &middot;
    {{ metric.summary.n_insufficient }} insufficient &middot;
    {{ metric.summary.n_total }} subgroups
  </p>
  {% if metric.summary.worst_subgroup %}
  <p class="dash-worst">
    Worst: <strong>{{ metric.summary.worst_subgroup.subgroup }}</strong>
    ({{ metric.summary.worst_subgroup.metric_value | fmt_num }},
    p={{ metric.summary.worst_subgroup.p_value | fmt_p }})
  </p>
  {% else %}
  <p class="dash-worst dash-worst-none">No flagged subgroup</p>
  {% endif %}
</div>
{%- endmacro %}

{% macro metric_table(metric) -%}
<table class="metric-table">
  <caption>{{ metric.label }} &mdash; by subgroup</caption>
  <thead>
    <tr>
      <th scope="col">Subgroup</th>
      <th scope="col">n</th>
      <th scope="col">Estimate</th>
      <th scope="col">95% CI</th>
      <th scope="col">p-value</th>
      <th scope="col">Status</th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    {% for row in metric.rows %}
    {% set status = row | status_class %}
    <tr class="{{ status }}">
      <td>{{ row.subgroup }}</td>
      <td>{{ row.subgroup_sample_size }}</td>
      <td>{{ row.metric_value | fmt_num }}</td>
      <td>{{ row | fmt_ci }}</td>
      <td>{{ row.p_value | fmt_p }}</td>
      <td>{{ status_badge(status) }}</td>
    </tr>
    {% endfor %}
  </tbody>
</table>
{%- endmacro %}

{% macro regulatory_section(metric) -%}
<div class="reg-mapping">
  <h4>Regulatory Mapping &mdash; EU AI Act Article 10</h4>
  {% if metric.regulatory %}
  <ul class="reg-list">
    {% for tag in metric.regulatory %}
    <li><span class="reg-badge">Art. {{ tag.article }}</span> {{ tag.note }}</li>
    {% endfor %}
  </ul>
  {% else %}
  <p class="reg-missing">No regulatory mapping supplied for this metric.</p>
  {% endif %}
</div>
{%- endmacro %}

{% macro shap_section(metric, shap_images) -%}
<div class="shap-block">
  <h4>Feature Attribution (SHAP)</h4>
  <div class="shap-grid">
    {% for row in metric.rows if (row | status_class) == "status-significant" %}
    {% set img_key = metric.key ~ "::" ~ row.subgroup %}
    <figure class="shap-figure">
      {% if img_key in shap_images %}
      <img src="{{ shap_images[img_key] }}"
           alt="SHAP attribution map for {{ row.subgroup }}, {{ metric.label }}">
      {% else %}
      <div class="shap-placeholder">SHAP image pending &mdash; {{ row.subgroup }}</div>
      {% endif %}
      <figcaption>{{ row.subgroup }}</figcaption>
    </figure>
    {% else %}
    <p class="shap-empty">No statistically significant disparities flagged for this metric.</p>
    {% endfor %}
  </div>
</div>
{%- endmacro %}

<header class="report-header">
  <h1>BiasAperture &mdash; Bias Audit Report</h1>
  <p class="scope-note">
    Diagnostic report only. This tool detects and reports demographic
    performance disparities; it does not retrain, debias, or modify the
    audited model.
  </p>
  <p class="meta-line">Generated {{ generated_at }} &middot; &alpha; = {{ alpha }}</p>
</header>

<section id="dashboard" class="dashboard-grid">
  {% for metric in metrics %}
  {{ dashboard_card(metric) }}
  {% endfor %}
</section>

{% for metric in metrics %}
<section class="metric-section" id="{{ metric.key }}">
  <h2>{{ metric.label }}</h2>
  {{ metric_table(metric) }}
  {{ regulatory_section(metric) }}
  {{ shap_section(metric, shap_images) }}
</section>
{% endfor %}

<footer class="report-footer">
  <p>
    "Pass/fail" indicators above are a scanning aid (no significant subgroup
    disparity found at &alpha;={{ alpha }}), not a standalone compliance
    verdict &mdash; refer to the full per-subgroup table, confidence
    intervals, and regulatory mapping for each metric before drawing a
    compliance conclusion.
  </p>
</footer>

</body>
</html>
```

Note: `inline_css` is passed into the render context as the raw contents of
`report/static/report.css` (read once in `generator.py`, no Jinja `{% include %}`
needed since it's plain CSS text, not a template).

---

## 6. Sample CSS — `report/static/report.css`

```css
:root {
  --color-bg: #ffffff;
  --color-text: #1a1a1a;
  --color-muted: #6b7280;
  --color-border: #e2e2e2;
  --color-fail-bg: #fdecea;
  --color-fail-text: #a13a30;
  --color-fail-border: #d64550;
  --color-pass-bg: #edf7ed;
  --color-pass-text: #2e7d32;
  --color-insuff-bg: #f2f2f2;
  --color-insuff-text: #6b7280;
  --font-sans: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, "Segoe UI", Roboto,
               Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; /* system stack — no @import,
               no Google Fonts, works fully offline */
}

* { box-sizing: border-box; }

body {
  font-family: var(--font-sans);
  color: var(--color-text);
  background: var(--color-bg);
  margin: 0;
  padding: 2rem;
  line-height: 1.5;
}

.report-header h1 { margin-bottom: 0.25rem; }
.scope-note { color: var(--color-muted); font-size: 0.9rem; max-width: 60ch; }
.meta-line { color: var(--color-muted); font-size: 0.85rem; }

.dashboard-grid {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(220px, 1fr));
  gap: 1rem;
  margin: 1.5rem 0 2rem;
}

.dash-card {
  border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
  border-left-width: 4px;
  border-radius: 6px;
  padding: 1rem;
}
.dash-card-fail { border-left-color: var(--color-fail-border); }
.dash-card-pass { border-left-color: var(--color-pass-text); }
.dash-card h3 { margin: 0 0 0.5rem; font-size: 1rem; }
.dash-card h3 a { color: inherit; text-decoration: none; }
.dash-meta, .dash-worst { font-size: 0.82rem; color: var(--color-muted); margin: 0.25rem 0; }

.badge {
  display: inline-block;
  padding: 0.15rem 0.5rem;
  border-radius: 999px;
  font-size: 0.78rem;
  font-weight: 600;
}
.badge-fail  { background: var(--color-fail-bg);  color: var(--color-fail-text); }
.badge-pass  { background: var(--color-pass-bg);  color: var(--color-pass-text); }
.badge-muted { background: var(--color-insuff-bg); color: var(--color-insuff-text); }

.metric-section { margin: 2.5rem 0; scroll-margin-top: 1rem; }

.metric-table {
  width: 100%;
  border-collapse: collapse;
  font-size: 0.9rem;
  margin: 1rem 0;
}
.metric-table caption { text-align: left; font-weight: 600; margin-bottom: 0.5rem; }
.metric-table th, .metric-table td {
  border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
  padding: 0.5rem 0.6rem;
  text-align: left;
}
.metric-table thead th { background: #fafafa; font-weight: 600; }

tr.status-significant  { background: var(--color-fail-bg); }
tr.status-insufficient { background: var(--color-insuff-bg); color: var(--color-insuff-text); }
tr.status-ok            { background: transparent; }

.reg-mapping { margin: 1rem 0; }
.reg-list { list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 0; }
.reg-list li { padding: 0.35rem 0; border-bottom: 1px dashed var(--color-border); font-size: 0.88rem; }
.reg-badge {
  display: inline-block;
  background: #eef2ff;
  color: #3730a3;
  border-radius: 4px;
  padding: 0.1rem 0.4rem;
  font-size: 0.78rem;
  margin-right: 0.4rem;
  font-family: ui-monospace, monospace;
}
.reg-missing { color: var(--color-muted); font-size: 0.85rem; font-style: italic; }

.shap-block { margin: 1rem 0; }
.shap-grid {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(180px, 1fr));
  gap: 1rem;
}
.shap-figure { margin: 0; text-align: center; }
.shap-figure img { max-width: 100%; border: 1px solid var(--color-border); border-radius: 4px; }
.shap-placeholder {
  border: 1px dashed var(--color-border);
  border-radius: 4px;
  padding: 2rem 1rem;
  color: var(--color-muted);
  font-size: 0.85rem;
}
.shap-figure figcaption { font-size: 0.78rem; color: var(--color-muted); margin-top: 0.3rem; }
.shap-empty { color: var(--color-muted); font-size: 0.85rem; font-style: italic; }

.report-footer {
  margin-top: 3rem;
  padding-top: 1rem;
  border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border);
  font-size: 0.8rem;
  color: var(--color-muted);
}

@media print {
  body { padding: 0.5in; }
  .dash-card, .metric-table, .shap-figure { break-inside: avoid; }
  .metric-section { page-break-before: auto; }
  a { color: inherit; text-decoration: none; }
}
```

