No change to `schema.py` is required or proposed — `MetricResult`'s existing
field set is sufficient for every rendering need in this design.

---

## 12. Sources / Precedent Patterns Consulted

- Jinja2 official design conventions (autoescape via `select_autoescape`,
  `trim_blocks`/`lstrip_blocks`, macro-based partials in a single template
  file) — standard, stable API, not version-sensitive.
- Base64 data-URI image inlining is the established pattern for "single
  self-contained HTML artifact" tooling (e.g., browser "Save as single
  file" extensions, Pandoc's `--self-contained`/`--embed-resources`
  output) — applied here to keep SHAP plots inside the one exported file.
- Regulatory/statistical framing (four-fifths-rule critique →
  never-bare-threshold design; NFR-003 flag-don't-fabricate) sourced from
  this project's own locked docs (`literature-review-matrix.md`,
  `BiasAperture-AT.md` §12, `schema-lock-m1.md`), not external search —
  already established ground truth for this repo.
